      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, there is a significant performance improvement for large repositories with a generated commit graph. For example, in the following setup:\n * Linux Kernel Repository\n * Commit Graph Generated\n * core.commitGraph \u003d true\n * HEAD only RevFilter\n * History View opened on the whole repository\n\nthen the GenerateHistoryJob runs for approximately 22 seconds if the raw bytes are always read. Most of that time (18.3 seconds) is spent in `RevWalk.getCachedBytes()`. Using this patch, that time is cut down to only 1.6 seconds.",
      "parentUuid": "1bf63351_76d3c2a6",
